OL,3,GNEWSANavy veterans compare Normandy
OL,4,Ainvasion stories
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo Royal Navy veterans who served
OL,7,Fduring World War Two have met for the
OL,8,Ffirst time to share memories of the
OL,9,Finvasion of Normandy in 1944.
OL,11,FRonald Hendrey, of Clacton-on-Sea in
OL,12,FEssex, was a gunner during D-Day, while
OL,13,FHenry Rice, from Cranleigh, Surrey,
OL,14,Fdelivered supplies to Juno Beach.
OL,16,FJay Hawkins, from St Ives,
OL,17,FCambridgeshire, introduced the
OL,18,Fcentenarians, as part of a project
OL,19,Fwhere he asks veterans to sign a rifle
OL,20,Fand records their wartime stories.
OL,23,APub: 30-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,375,370,200,160,0,100
